<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăgĭlĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		agilis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the condition of</i> agilis, <i>mobility</i>,
				<i>nimbleness</i>, <i>activity</i>,
				<i>quickness</i>, <i>fleetness</i>,
				<i>agility.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: navium, 
			<i><span class="en">Liv. 26,
				51</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rotarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt. 4,
					6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cursus et agilitas alicujus,</span>”
				<i>mobility</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 180</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: agilitas, ut ita dicam, mollitiaque
			naturae, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 1, 17, 4</span></i>.</div>
